  "facts": [
    "Trace.dropped defaults to None; is_dropped tests is-not-None, and drop preserves the first reason, including an empty reason. ok/error status is independent of dropped. Reward aggregation still sums non-None rewards, including any recorded before a drop; empty rewards still aggregate to zero.",
    "Criterion.drop contains unscored answers, disjoint from scored choices. Choices scores must be finite; duplicate drop answers and fewer than two total answers are rejected. A drop applies regardless of criterion weight. RubricJudge records per-answer metrics, sets the reason and returns None before weighted aggregation.",
    "Task.score skips recording reward/judge values that are None. It does not generally turn None into dropped. AgenticJudgeEnv propagates a configured drop to the solver trace and returns before judge reward recording.",
    "scoring_transaction snapshots/restores dropped with state/rewards/metrics/info on BaseException. Isolated grade_task copies result.dropped back only after grading/on_score completes. Task.rescore first refuses errored traces, then clears prior rewards/metrics/extra_usage and dropped before rescoring.",
    "UnscoredError is removed from errors/exports and the old post-scoring NaN-to-None path is removed. Trace.record_reward rejects a nonfinite value. Historical #2949/weighted-NaN observations remain facts about their pinned earlier versions.",
    "format_mean filters dropped traces before computing clean/global means. Replay displays dropped; serve deltas include dropped. This commit changes no trainer file. The PR explicitly asks prime-rl iter_trainable_traces consumers to filter dropped before adopting this version.",
    "Four new unit test functions cover rubric drop metrics, selected criterion validation, NaN reward rejection and scoring-transaction drop rollback. No new complete rollout/resume/trainer or isolated-grading test is added in the sixteen-file commit."
  ],
  "author_assertions": [
    "221 unit tests passed, nine skipped, style/type checks clean: author report only, not our execution or CI-log review.",
    "Live private repoforge-harbor isolated-grading rollout remained ok/dropped without audit/judge reward; private run and model service are not independently accessible/verified here.",
    "Dropped traces are not retried and resume keeps them: author claim; full retry/resume consumers outside changed code were not independently reviewed."
  ],
  "our_inference": "Runner acceptance must version dropped separately from ok/error/scoring_skipped/reward presence and test actual training admission. A successful scalar zero or ok alone cannot establish scored correctness or trainability. Excluding dropped examples changes the denominator and can bias apparent quality if workload/reason mix changes.",
  "next_falsifiable_gate": "Freeze authentic pre/post runner, rubric/drop policy, trainer filter, workload IDs and resource ceiling. Exercise scored-zero, finite score, None-without-drop, policy skip, explicit drop (including zero-weight and prior reward), nonfinite failure, shared rollback, isolated commit/failure, replay and two process recoveries. Record attempted/scored/skipped/dropped/failed and admitted-to-training memberships with intersections rather than assuming disjoint counts; require no dropped training member or duplicate score/effect and invariant versioned denominators. Existing real wire/token/mask/score and H1/H2/H3 gates remain unmet.",
  "limitations": [
    "Source inspection only: no local upstream import/test/runtime/provider/model/training/GPU execution, no author private-run reproduction or CI-log/test-selection review.",
    "Full sixteen parent/landed file pairs and exact patches verified; downstream trainer and unchanged retry/resume paths not fully reviewed.",
    "No throughput, production reliability, model quality, novelty or scientific-status upgrade. No full upstream implementation redistributed."
  ],
